<http://data.silknow.org/event/c6feae4c-ace9-3169-a41a-09a2e04ba804>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This box contains the initals P.M. This can be traced to Parnell Mackett whose work, with that of her sisters, can be traced to the family from which the work box came. Elizabeth Mackett's sampler is also in the V&A (433-1884), and Parnell Mackett sampler is at the Art Institute, Chicago.\n\nThis was purchased from Miss I M Arnold Forster for £75 in 1926."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/3c97bab2-f2e3-355b-8bec-2d9cb47df794> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This box contains the initals P.M. This can be traced to Parnell Mackett whose work, with that of her sisters, can be traced to the family from which the work box came. Elizabeth Mackett's sampler is also in the V&A (433-1884), and Parnell Mackett sampler is at the Art Institute, Chicago.\n\nThis was purchased from Miss I M Arnold Forster for £75 in 1926."@en .

